        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Confirm Implemented Clause Update",
            "prompt": "You are generating the post-implementation clause update confirmation as plain markdown.\n\nReturn markdown only. Do not return oraInfoDisplay blocks, oraInsight blocks, XML, JSON, or code fences.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nPREPARED: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_IMPLEMENT_RECOMMENDATION_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}.\nAPPLY_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.APPLY_IMPLEMENT_RECOMMENDATION_UPDATES.$output}}.\nCLAUSE_TEXT_UPDATE_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_CONTRACT_CLAUSE_TEXT_BY_TITLE.$output}}.\n\nDATA RESOLUTION RULES:\n- Use clause title from PREPARED.clauseTitle, then ACTION_CONTEXT.clauseTitle, then `Clause`.\n- Use current contract language from PREPARED.originalClauseText, then ACTION_CONTEXT.originalClauseText.\n- Use updated clause language from PREPARED.proposedClauseText, then ACTION_CONTEXT.proposedClauseText.\n- Semantics are strict:\n  - `ContractDeviatingClause.OriginalClauseText` = current clause language in contract.\n  - `ContractDeviatingClause.ProposedClauseText` = updated proposed language.\n- If either clause text is missing, still return valid markdown with safe fallback wording.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (exact shape):\n# <clauseTitle> clause updated with proposed language\n\nKey Updates\n- <difference bullets>\n\nRULES:\n- Heading must be exactly `# <clauseTitle> clause updated with proposed language`.\n- Render `Key Updates` exactly as plain text section label (not a heading).\n- Bullets must compare OriginalClauseText vs ProposedClauseText only.\n- Bullet count is difference-driven: include all meaningful differences and do not enforce a fixed minimum or maximum.\n- Each bullet must map to a concrete left-vs-right text delta (for example numbers, dates, durations, obligations, limits, approvals, thresholds, scope).\n- Do not include unchanged-context bullets or retention statements.\n- Never use wording such as retained, unchanged, remains, still, no change, or equivalent no-delta phrasing.\n- If there are no meaningful differences, return exactly one bullet:\n  - `No material differences found between current and proposed language.`\n- If one or more meaningful differences exist, do not output the no-difference fallback bullet.\n- Do not include additional sections or text outside this format."
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CONFIRM_IMPLEMENTED_CLAUSE_UPDATE",
          "id": "1777437087637",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777437087641_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating the post-implementation clause update confirmation as plain markdown.\n\nReturn markdown only. Do not return oraInfoDisplay blocks, oraInsight blocks, XML, JSON, or code fences.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nPREPARED: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_IMPLEMENT_RECOMMENDATION_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}.\nAPPLY_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.APPLY_IMPLEMENT_RECOMMENDATION_UPDATES.$output}}.\nCLAUSE_TEXT_UPDATE_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_CONTRACT_CLAUSE_TEXT_BY_TITLE.$output}}.\n\nDATA RESOLUTION RULES:\n- Use clause title from PREPARED.clauseTitle, then ACTION_CONTEXT.clauseTitle, then `Clause`.\n- Use current contract language from PREPARED.originalClauseText, then ACTION_CONTEXT.originalClauseText.\n- Use updated clause language from PREPARED.proposedClauseText, then ACTION_CONTEXT.proposedClauseText.\n- Semantics are strict:\n  - `ContractDeviatingClause.OriginalClauseText` = current clause language in contract.\n  - `ContractDeviatingClause.ProposedClauseText` = updated proposed language.\n- If either clause text is missing, still return valid markdown with safe fallback wording.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (exact shape):\n# <clauseTitle> clause updated with proposed language\n\nKey Updates\n- <difference bullets>\n\nRULES:\n- Heading must be exactly `# <clauseTitle> clause updated with proposed language`.\n- Render `Key Updates` exactly as plain text section label (not a heading).\n- Bullets must compare OriginalClauseText vs ProposedClauseText only.\n- Bullet count is difference-driven: include all meaningful differences and do not enforce a fixed minimum or maximum.\n- Each bullet must map to a concrete left-vs-right text delta (for example numbers, dates, durations, obligations, limits, approvals, thresholds, scope).\n- Do not include unchanged-context bullets or retention statements.\n- Never use wording such as retained, unchanged, remains, still, no change, or equivalent no-delta phrasing.\n- If there are no meaningful differences, return exactly one bullet:\n  - `No material differences found between current and proposed language.`\n- If one or more meaningful differences exist, do not output the no-difference fallback bullet.\n- Do not include additional sections or text outside this format."
            }
          ],
