              "id": "18_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a recommendation review response with one message list and one insight action.\n\nReturn only the required plain-text summary plus valid UI output blocks. Do not return markdown.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nDATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_POLICY_RECOMMENDATION_MESSAGES.$output.result}}.\n\nID AND COMMAND INTEGRITY:\n- Treat contractId, deviatingClauseId, policyDeviationId, recommendationId, allRecommendationIds, siblingRecommendationIds, implementationTargets, and every form id as opaque strings.\n- Copy these values exactly from DATA, ACTION_CONTEXT, PREPARED, row prepared payload fields, or prepared command strings.\n- Never shorten, reformat, convert to numbers, infer, sort, or rebuild IDs or ID arrays from surrounding text.\n- If a prepared command string is provided, use it character-for-character.\n- Only generate display text, summaries, topics, rejection reasons, and proposed clause language where explicitly allowed.\n- Copy prepared `priority`, `statusPriority`, and `severityPriority` values exactly where referenced; do not infer or remap them from severity/status text, lookup meanings, recommendation type, title, or summary, and preserve `neutral` when provided.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT AND ORDER:\n1. First output must be plain text only and must be exactly DATA.sectionDescription.\n2. Second output must be exactly one <oraInfoDisplay key=\"policy_recommendations\"> block containing JSON for `messageListWidget`.\n3. Third output must be exactly one <oraInsight> block.\n4. Do not output any extra text before the plain-text summary, between blocks, or after the insight block.\n5. The first plain-text summary must not be wrapped in quotes, XML tags, JSON, markdown, or code fences.\n6. Every UI block must be raw, not markdown fenced/quoted/CDATA-wrapped, and must contain one complete valid JSON object with escaped quotes/newlines in string values and command payloads.\n\nMESSAGE LIST JSON AND ITEM RULES:\n- The info display JSON must contain `\"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\"` exactly and use the local top-level wrapper shape (`title`, `patternId`, optional `description`, and `properties`); do not use `config`:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"<LLM-generated one-line section title>\",\n    \"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\",\n    \"description\": \"<copy DATA.sectionDescription exactly>\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"subtitle\": \"<copy DATA.sectionDescription exactly>\",\n      \"summary\": \"<copy DATA.sectionDescription exactly>\",\n      \"items\": [ ... ]\n    }\n  }\n- `properties.items` must be an array of item objects.\n- Each item must include `title`.\n- Supported item fields are only: `title`, `subtitle`, `summary`, `status`, `statusPriority`, `badgeText`, `priority`, `timestamp`, `action`, `additionalAction`, and `image`.\n- Omit empty optional fields instead of outputting null, empty objects, or unsupported fields.\n- Include `image` only when the source DATA/PREPARED item provides a non-empty image URL or path. Do not invent image URLs, and do not use emoji or Unicode icons as image substitutes.\n- Generate `title` in one crisp line (max 18 words) using DATA.sectionTitleContext:\n  - include request party context from DATA.sectionTitleContext.requestParty (Supplier or Customer).\n  - include what they are trying to change from DATA.sectionTitleContext.issueText.\n  - keep it concise and business-readable.\n  - prefer phrasing like `<Party> deviates ...`.\n- `description` must be exactly DATA.sectionDescription.\n- `properties.subtitle` must be exactly DATA.sectionDescription.\n- `properties.summary` must be exactly DATA.sectionDescription.\n- Use DATA.items as source rows and preserve DATA.items order exactly.\n- DATA.items order is strict: Standard first, then Fallback 1..n in numeric order, then Out-of-policy, then the intent request row (Supplier request for buy, Customer request for sell).\n- DATA.sectionDescription is prepared by code. It either says to select the position for the Supplier/Customer Request or states the previously accepted position. Copy it exactly; do not paraphrase it.\n- Recommendation type labels are already display-ready in DATA. Keep fallback labels human-readable, such as Fallback 1 or Fallback 44. Do not output FALLBACK_1, FALLBACK_44, or similar code-style labels.\n- For each row item:\n  - Keep `title` exactly as provided in DATA.items[].title.\n  - Generate `summary` in one crisp single-line sentence from DATA.items[].summary.\n  - `badgeText` must be a short text label. Do not use a badge object in a messageListWidget item.\n  - Keep `badgeText` exactly from DATA.\n  - Keep `priority` exactly from DATA.\n  - Valid `priority` and `statusPriority` values are: `alert`, `warning`, `medium`, `success`, `neutral`.\n  - Copy each prepared item `priority` and `statusPriority` exactly; do not swap them or recalculate them.\n  - Copy each prepared item `priority` and `statusPriority` exactly; do not swap them or recalculate them.\n  - Severity badge priority mapping is strict and must already be reflected in DATA from exact lookup codes: 4_CRITICAL -> \"alert\"; 3_HIGH_RISK -> \"warning\"; 2_MEDIUM_RISK -> \"medium\"; 1_LOW_RISK -> \"neutral\"; 0_NO_RISK -> \"success\". SeverityCode is already the lookup code; do not normalize meaning text to derive priority.\n  - Do not infer, replace, or remap badge priority values in the prompt output.\n  - `statusPriority` styles the `status` text only; item badge styling comes from `priority`.\n  - Preserve `status` exactly when provided (for example `Supplier Requested`, `Customer Requested`, `Closely matches to supplier request`, or `Closely matches to customer request`).\n  - Preserve `statusPriority` exactly when provided; do not replace it with `priority`.\n  - Include `status` only when DATA.items[].status is non-empty.\n  - Include `statusPriority` only when DATA.items[].statusPriority is non-empty.\n  - Do not infer `status` or `statusPriority` from title, recommendationTypeCode, requestParty, matchedPositionCode, or sectionDescription.\n  - If the row title is `Supplier request` or `Customer request` and DATA does not provide `status`, do not output `Supplier Requested` or `Customer Requested`.\n  - Request recommendation rows must keep `statusPriority`: `warning` when DATA provides it. Do not add icon, emoji, or Unicode warning/check/info/exclamation symbols.\n  - Severity badge color is separate: keep badge `priority` from DATA even when `statusPriority` is warning.\n  - Preserve `actionState` exactly when provided.\n  - `additionalAction`, when present, must contain only `text` and `command`.\n  - Preserve `additionalAction` exactly as provided in DATA when present.\n  - If a row does not include `additionalAction`, do not synthesize or add an action.\n  - Preserve prepared `action` and `additionalAction.command` strings exactly. Do not rebuild command payloads.\n  - For Accept actions where DATA.items[].additionalAction.command is non-empty, preserve the command verbatim; do not rewrite command payload fields.\n  - When DATA.items[].additionalAction.command is non-empty, it must remain exactly one of: ora.Invoke('SendAgentCommandRefresh',...) or ora.Invoke('SendAgentCommandNoRefresh',...) as already provided in DATA.\n  - Do not add unsupported fields.\n\nINSIGHT RULES:\n- Return exactly one insight.\n- `title` must be exactly DATA.rejectActionLabel.\n- `actionText` must be exactly DATA.rejectActionLabel.\n- DATA.rejectActionLabel is intent-based: Buy/B -> `Reject Supplier Request`; Sell/S -> `Reject Customer Request`.\n- `shortDescription` must be one concise sentence indicating the request will be rejected for this policy deviation issue.\n- `followUpCommand` must be exactly in this command format:\n  ora.Invoke('RejectRecommendation', <payload-object>)\n- Build the payload object by copying DATA.rejectFormPayloadBase exactly, then add exactly one generated key:\n  - \"value\": \"<LLM-generated rejection reason using DATA.issueText and request party derived from DATA.BuyOrSell: Supplier when B/BUY, Customer when S/SELL>\"\n- Do not rebuild or modify DATA.rejectFormPayloadBase.id.\n- Generate `value` as one concise professional sentence.\n- The `value` sentence must clearly state why the requested clause change conflicts with company policy.\n\nEMPTY STATE:\n- If DATA.items is empty, return one item: { \"title\": \"No recommendations available\", \"summary\": \"No recommendation options are available for this policy deviation.\" }."
