          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "customNotes": "Use exactly one multiRecordWidget info display. patternId must be \"multiRecordWidget\". Keep title empty. Use properties.cols and properties.rows only, with row objects containing cells and optional action. Severity and Status cells must be badge objects with priority alert, warning, medium, success, or neutral; never quoted JSON strings. Do not use image or message-list item fields. Copy row.severityPriority and row.statusPriority exactly from DATA; do not recalculate or remap badge priorities. Each multiRecord row must have exactly 5 cells matching the columns; Severity and Status appear only as their badge cells, never as duplicate string cells."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Display Clause Deviations",
            "prompt": "CONTEXT: Contract number is {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.contractNumber}}. SUMMARY_DATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.initDisplaySummaryRows || []}}. TABLE_DATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.initDisplayTableRows || $context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.initDisplayLlmRows || $context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.initDisplayRows || $context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.rows}}.\n\nTASK: Generate the startup display for the contract clause deviations review screen.\n\nID AND COMMAND INTEGRITY:\n- Treat every reviewInvokeCommand value as an opaque prepared command string.\n- Copy reviewInvokeCommand exactly for the row Review action; never rebuild it from IDs, actionPayload, or surrounding text.\n- Do not expose hidden IDs or policy issue metadata in visible text unless the field is explicitly used by the display rules.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT AND ORDER:\n1. If SUMMARY_DATA has rows, first output exactly one concise plain-text summary sentence.\n2. If SUMMARY_DATA is empty, omit the summary and start directly with the <oraInfoDisplay> block.\n3. After the optional summary, return exactly one <oraInfoDisplay key=\"clause_deviations\"> block containing JSON for `multiRecordWidget`.\n4. Do not output any extra text before the optional summary, between the optional summary and the first <oraInfoDisplay> block, or after the block.\n5. The optional plain-text summary must not be wrapped in quotes, XML tags, JSON, markdown, or code fences.\n6. The info display JSON must contain `\"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\"` exactly and must not include top-level `description`, `subtitle`, `properties.subtitle`, or `properties.summary`; the optional leading plain-text summary is the panel summary.\n7. The oraInfoDisplay block must be raw, not markdown fenced/quoted/CDATA-wrapped, and must contain one complete valid JSON object with escaped quotes/newlines in string values and command payloads.\n\nSUMMARY SELECTION RULES:\n- Generate the leading summary using SUMMARY_DATA only.\n- SUMMARY_DATA contains at most the first 2 already-ordered clauses that have open Critical policy issues.\n- If SUMMARY_DATA has rows, output exactly 1 concise sentence.\n- The summary should not repeat Requested Changes text already shown in the table.\n- Mention only the clause titles and that open critical policy issues need attention.\n- Do not include policy issue details, requested-change details, deviationSummary, issue text, or changeRequestSummary in the summary.\n- If SUMMARY_DATA is empty, do not output any summary text.\n- Do not use TABLE_DATA, row-level statusDisplay, row-level severityDisplay, deviationSummary, or standardPositionSummary to create fallback summary text.\n- Do not mention more than 2 clauses in the summary.\n- Do not invent issue details, severities, statuses, or clause titles not present in SUMMARY_DATA.\n- The summary rule applies only to the optional leading plain-text summary; it must not limit, filter, or reorder the table rows.\n\nMULTI-RECORD DISPLAY RULES:\n- The widget JSON must use the local top-level wrapper shape (`title`, `patternId`, optional `description`, and `properties`), no `config`, and no unsupported table fields:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"\",\n    \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"cols\": [\"Clause\", \"Requested Changes\", \"Severity\", \"Standard Position\", \"Status\"],\n      \"rows\": [\n        {\n          \"cells\": [\n            \"<clauseTitle>\",\n            \"<requestedChanges>\",\n            { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"<severityDisplay>\", \"priority\": \"<severityPriority>\" },\n            \"<standardPosition>\",\n            { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"<statusDisplay>\", \"priority\": \"<statusPriority>\" }\n          ],\n          \"action\": { \"text\": \"Review\", \"command\": \"<row.reviewInvokeCommand>\" }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n- In the multiRecordWidget, render exactly one table row for every object in TABLE_DATA.\n- Do not filter, limit, summarize away, or drop TABLE_DATA rows from the table based on summary prioritization, severity, status, or policyIssues.\n- Preserve TABLE_DATA order for the table rows unless another display rule explicitly defines a different order.\n- Keep title empty (\"\"). Do not add any other title or subtitle.\n- Render columns in this exact order: Clause, Requested Changes, Severity, Standard Position, Status.\n- Rows must be row objects with a `cells` array. Do not output raw cell arrays.\n- The number of cells in each row must exactly match the number of columns.\n- Each row.cells array must contain exactly 5 entries in this order: Clause, Requested Changes, Severity badge, Standard Position, Status badge; do not append extra cells after the Status badge.\n- Use row values clauseTitle, deviationSummary, severityDisplay, standardPositionSummary, and statusDisplay.\n- For Requested Changes and Standard Position columns, summarize each row value to concise 2-4 lines while preserving the core meaning.\n- Severity and Status cells must be badge objects, not quoted JSON strings.\n- Never output row.severityDisplay or row.statusDisplay as standalone string cells; they may appear only inside the corresponding badge object `text` field.\n- Render Severity as a badge object using TABLE_DATA fields exactly:\n  { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": row.severityDisplay, \"priority\": row.severityPriority }.\n- Render Status as a badge object using TABLE_DATA fields exactly:\n  { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": row.statusDisplay, \"priority\": row.statusPriority }.\n- Badge priority must be one of: `alert`, `warning`, `medium`, `success`, `neutral`.\n- TABLE_DATA already includes the final badge priority values in row.severityPriority and row.statusPriority. Do not recalculate, infer, replace, or remap them.\n- Copy prepared row `severityPriority` and `statusPriority` exactly into badge priorities; do not swap or recalculate them.\n- Exact severity lookup-code mapping used by TABLE_DATA is: 4_CRITICAL -> \"alert\"; 3_HIGH_RISK -> \"warning\"; 2_MEDIUM_RISK -> \"medium\"; 1_LOW_RISK -> \"neutral\"; 0_NO_RISK -> \"success\". SeverityCode is already the lookup code; do not normalize meaning text to derive priority.\n- Add row `action` as { \"text\": \"Review\", \"command\": \"<row.reviewInvokeCommand>\" }, copying row.reviewInvokeCommand exactly.\n- Do not include `image`, `badgeText`, `status`, `statusPriority`, `additionalAction`, `drillDownAction`, or message-list-only item fields in multiRecordWidget rows.\n- Do not include policyIssues in the table.\n\nEMPTY STATE:\n- If TABLE_DATA is missing, empty, or has no rows, return exactly one empty multiRecordWidget with the same columns and an empty rows array.\n- Do not output a leading summary in the empty state.\n- The info display must still use key \"clause_deviations\", title \"\", patternId \"multiRecordWidget\", and properties.cols [\"Clause\", \"Requested Changes\", \"Severity\", \"Standard Position\", \"Status\"].\n- In the empty-state widget, set properties.rows to [] exactly. Do not add placeholder rows, actions, subtitles, descriptions, or unsupported fields.",
            "appExperience": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "customNotes": "Use exactly one multiRecordWidget info display. patternId must be \"multiRecordWidget\". Keep title empty. Use properties.cols and properties.rows only, with row objects containing cells and optional action. Severity and Status cells must be badge objects with priority alert, warning, medium, success, or neutral; never quoted JSON strings. Do not use image or message-list item fields. Copy row.severityPriority and row.statusPriority exactly from TABLE_DATA; do not recalculate or remap badge priorities. Each multiRecord row must have exactly 5 cells matching the columns; Severity and Status appear only as their badge cells, never as duplicate string cells."
            }
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
