          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Actions Clause Deviations",
            "prompt": "DATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CLAUSE_DEVIATIONS.$output.result.initActionPolicyDeviationRows}}.\n\nID AND COMMAND INTEGRITY:\n- Treat contractId, deviatingClauseId, policyDeviationId, and every prepared payload field as opaque strings.\n- Copy IDs and prepared command strings exactly from DATA.\n- If a prepared command string is provided, use it character-for-character.\nTASK: Generate up to three InitActions for open critical policy deviations only. DATA is already filtered to Critical rows only, sorted by open clause priority, and limited to the first three eligible open critical policy deviations.\nOUTPUT: Return oraInsight items only.\nRULES:\n- Use rows from DATA in order; do not add rows that are not in DATA.\n- Only Critical policy deviations are eligible for InitActions; do not add High risk, Medium risk, Low risk, No risk, blank, or unknown severity rows.\n- Set each oraInsight `title` exactly to DATA[].insightTitle. Do not prefix with `Review`, do not prefix with severity, and do not append `Clause`.\n- Generate `shortDescription` from DATA[].changeRequestSummary as a very small 2-7 word phrase.\n- The phrase must name the changed business subject and the requested action from the same DATA row.\n- When the row includes a concrete value, amount, percentage, date, period, cap, or threshold, preserve that value in the phrase.\n- Prefer the shape `<value> <business subject>` or `<action> <business subject>`.\n- If the row has multiple values, choose the value tied to the primary changed subject in that row.\n- If the row is a wording-only change without concrete values, summarize the changed business subject and wording action, such as `Revise notice obligation`, `Update shipping language`, or `Clarify delivery timing`.\n- Set `actionText` exactly to DATA[].insightActionText, which must be `View Options`.\n- Set `followUpCommand` exactly to DATA[].insightFollowUpCommand.\n- Set `priority` exactly to DATA[].insightPriority.\n- Set `priorityLevel` exactly to DATA[].insightPriorityLevel.\n- The followUpCommand must use `ora.Invoke('SendAgentCommandNoRefresh',...)`; do not use `ora.Agent(...)`.\n- Do not use DATA[].agentReviewCommand, `Review`, or `ViewDeviations` for InitActions.\n- Do not rebuild the command from `viewOptionsPayload`; copy the prepared command string without changing IDs or action values.\n- Escape quotation marks inside JSON string values, and copy prepared followUpCommand and priority fields exactly.\n- If DATA is empty, return no actions.\n- Output only raw oraInsight blocks; each block must contain exactly one valid JSON object, with no markdown fences, prose, labels, JSON arrays, or text before/between/after blocks."
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
