          "id": "19",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "19_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating the post-acceptance confirmation as plain markdown.\n\nReturn markdown only. Do not return oraInfoDisplay blocks, oraInsight blocks, XML, JSON, or code fences.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nPREPARED: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_ACCEPT_RECOMMENDATION_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}.\nAPPLY_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.APPLY_ACCEPT_RECOMMENDATION_UPDATES.$output}}.\n\nDATA RESOLUTION RULES:\n- Resolve accepted recommendation record from APPLY_RESULT parts item id `fetchAcceptedRecommendation`.\n- Get `RecommendationType` from that record.\n- Get `PositionText` from that record.\n- Topic must come from PREPARED.topic, then ACTION_CONTEXT.topic.\n- If accepted record PositionText is unavailable, use the default missing-position fallback sentence below.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (exact shape):\n# <recommendationType> accepted for <topic>\n\n<acceptanceSummaryFromPositionText>\n\nRULES:\n- The first line must be a markdown heading exactly in the format: `# <recommendationType> accepted for <topic>`.\n- Humanize `<recommendationType>` for display: convert code-like tokens to readable Title Case words.\n- Replace underscores/hyphens with spaces in `<recommendationType>` and preserve numbers as separate tokens.\n- Example: `FALLBACK_1` must become `Fallback 1`; `OUT_OF_POLICY` must become `Out Of Policy`.\n- The second line must be one concise LLM-generated sentence based on `<positionText>`.\n- The second line must clearly describe the clause state after acceptance and include the phrase `after acceptance`.\n- Do not copy `<positionText>` verbatim unless it is already concise and clear.\n- If topic is missing, use `this clause`.\n- If recommendation type is missing, use `Recommendation`.\n- If position text is missing, use exactly: `The selected recommendation applies after acceptance.`\n- Do not include any additional sections or extra text."
            },
