                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "customNotes": "Use exactly one messageListWidget info display. patternId must be \"messageListWidget\". Items must use only supported message-list fields: title, subtitle, summary, status, statusPriority, badgeText, priority, timestamp, action, additionalAction, image. Do not use badge objects in message-list items. Use image only when provided by DATA/PREPARED; do not invent icons or image URLs. Render the saved rejection response as a plain-text summary, one message list info display, one Edit Reason insight that reopens RejectRecommendation with the current reason, and one immediate RefreshPanel invoke. Copy prepared rejection summary, messageListWidget fields, edit command, and RefreshPanel immediate insight exactly."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Confirm Reject Issue",
            "prompt": "You are generating the post-rejection response after saving the rejection reason.\n\nReturn only the required plain-text summary plus valid UI output blocks. Do not return markdown.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nPREPARED: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_REJECT_ISSUE_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}.\nUPDATE_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.APPLY_REJECT_ISSUE_UPDATES.$output}}.\n\nID AND COMMAND INTEGRITY:\n- Treat contractId, deviatingClauseId, policyDeviationId, recommendationId, allRecommendationIds, siblingRecommendationIds, implementationTargets, and every form id as opaque strings.\n- Copy these values exactly from DATA, ACTION_CONTEXT, PREPARED, row prepared payload fields, or prepared command strings.\n- Never shorten, reformat, convert to numbers, infer, sort, or rebuild IDs or ID arrays from surrounding text.\n- If a prepared command string is provided, use it character-for-character.\n- Only generate display text, summaries, topics, rejection reasons, and proposed clause language where explicitly allowed.\n- Copy prepared `priority` and `statusPriority` values exactly where referenced; do not infer or remap them from severity/status text, lookup meanings, recommendation type, title, or summary, and preserve `neutral` when provided.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT AND ORDER:\n1. First output must be plain text only and must be exactly PREPARED.rejectionSummary.\n2. Second output must be exactly one <oraInfoDisplay key=\"policy_rejection\"> block containing JSON for `messageListWidget`.\n3. Third output must be exactly one <oraInsight> block for Edit Reason.\n4. Fourth output must be exactly one <oraImmediateInsight> block that invokes the app-level RefreshPanel action.\n5. Do not output any extra text before the plain-text summary, between blocks, or after the immediate insight block.\n6. The first plain-text summary must not be wrapped in quotes, XML tags, JSON, markdown, or code fences.\n7. Every UI block must be raw, not markdown fenced/quoted/CDATA-wrapped, and must contain one complete valid JSON object with escaped quotes/newlines in string values and command payloads.\n\nMESSAGE LIST JSON AND ITEM RULES:\n- The info display JSON must contain `\"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\"` exactly and use the local top-level wrapper shape (`title`, `patternId`, optional `description`, and `properties`); do not use `config`:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"<topic> reviewed\",\n    \"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\",\n    \"description\": \"<PREPARED.rejectionSummary>\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"subtitle\": \"<PREPARED.rejectSubtitle>\",\n      \"summary\": \"<PREPARED.rejectionSummary>\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Rejection reason\",\n          \"summary\": \"<rejectionReason>\",\n          \"priority\": \"warning\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n- `properties.items` must be an array of item objects.\n- Each item must include `title`.\n- Supported item fields are only: `title`, `subtitle`, `summary`, `status`, `statusPriority`, `badgeText`, `priority`, `timestamp`, `action`, `additionalAction`, and `image`.\n- Valid `priority` and `statusPriority` values are: `alert`, `warning`, `medium`, `success`, `neutral`.\n- Copy each prepared `priority` and `statusPriority` exactly where used; do not swap or recalculate them.\n- `badgeText` must be a short text label. Do not use a badge object in a messageListWidget item.\n- `statusPriority` styles the `status` text only; item badge styling comes from `priority`.\n- `additionalAction`, when present, must contain only `text` and `command`.\n- Preserve prepared `action` and `additionalAction.command` strings exactly. Do not rebuild command payloads.\n- Include `image` only when the source DATA/PREPARED item provides a non-empty image URL or path. Do not invent image URLs, and do not use emoji or Unicode icons as image substitutes.\n- Omit empty optional fields instead of outputting null, empty objects, or unsupported fields.\n- <topic> must be 2 to 4 words in Title Case derived from ChangeRequestSummary.\n- Derive ChangeRequestSummary from these sources in order:\n  1) UPDATE_RESULT parts item `fetchRejectedPolicyDeviation` -> payload/result -> ChangeRequestSummary\n  2) PREPARED.changeRequestSummary\n  3) ACTION_CONTEXT.changeRequestSummary\n  4) ACTION_CONTEXT.issueText\n- description and properties.summary must exactly equal PREPARED.rejectionSummary.\n- properties.subtitle must exactly equal PREPARED.rejectSubtitle when present.\n- <rejectionReason> must use the exact submitted editor text from ACTION_CONTEXT.newValue when available; otherwise use PREPARED.rejectionReason.\n- Do not add unsupported fields.\n\nEDIT REASON INSIGHT RULES:\n- Return exactly one ordinary insight after the policy_rejection info display and before the immediate insight.\n- `title` must be exactly `Edit Reason`.\n- `actionText` must be exactly `Edit Reason`.\n- `shortDescription` must be one concise sentence saying the rejection reason can be updated.\n- `followUpCommand` must be exactly in this command format:\n  ora.Invoke('RejectRecommendation', <payload-object>)\n- Build the payload object by copying PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase exactly, then add exactly one key:\n  - \"value\": \"<current rejection reason>\"\n- <current rejection reason> must use the exact submitted editor text from ACTION_CONTEXT.newValue when available; otherwise use PREPARED.rejectionReason.\n- Do not rebuild or modify PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase.id.\n- Do not change the form id, type, title, subtitle, or commitText from PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase.\n- Saving the reopened form must return to the same reject update and CONFIRM_REJECT_ISSUE confirmation flow.\n\nIMMEDIATE REFRESH RULES:\n- Return exactly one immediate insight after the Edit Reason insight.\n- The immediate insight must be exactly:\n<oraImmediateInsight>\n{\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"RefreshPanel\\\")\"\n}\n</oraImmediateInsight>\n- Do not add title, shortDescription, actionText, or any other fields to the immediate insight.\n- Do not change the RefreshPanel action code.",
            "systemPrompt": "You output a plain-text rejection summary, one messageListWidget info display, one Edit Reason insight that reopens the rejection form with the current reason, and one immediate RefreshPanel invoke after reject update is saved. Use PREPARED.rejectionSummary for buy/sell aware wording and preserve IDs exactly."
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CONFIRM_REJECT_ISSUE",
          "id": "20",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "20_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating the post-rejection response after saving the rejection reason.\n\nReturn only the required plain-text summary plus valid UI output blocks. Do not return markdown.\n\nACTION_CONTEXT: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output.result}}.\nPREPARED: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_REJECT_ISSUE_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}.\nUPDATE_RESULT: {{$context.$nodes.APPLY_REJECT_ISSUE_UPDATES.$output}}.\n\nID AND COMMAND INTEGRITY:\n- Treat contractId, deviatingClauseId, policyDeviationId, recommendationId, allRecommendationIds, siblingRecommendationIds, implementationTargets, and every form id as opaque strings.\n- Copy these values exactly from DATA, ACTION_CONTEXT, PREPARED, row prepared payload fields, or prepared command strings.\n- Never shorten, reformat, convert to numbers, infer, sort, or rebuild IDs or ID arrays from surrounding text.\n- If a prepared command string is provided, use it character-for-character.\n- Only generate display text, summaries, topics, rejection reasons, and proposed clause language where explicitly allowed.\n- Copy prepared `priority` and `statusPriority` values exactly where referenced; do not infer or remap them from severity/status text, lookup meanings, recommendation type, title, or summary, and preserve `neutral` when provided.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT AND ORDER:\n1. First output must be plain text only and must be exactly PREPARED.rejectionSummary.\n2. Second output must be exactly one <oraInfoDisplay key=\"policy_rejection\"> block containing JSON for `messageListWidget`.\n3. Third output must be exactly one <oraInsight> block for Edit Reason.\n4. Fourth output must be exactly one <oraImmediateInsight> block that invokes the app-level RefreshPanel action.\n5. Do not output any extra text before the plain-text summary, between blocks, or after the immediate insight block.\n6. The first plain-text summary must not be wrapped in quotes, XML tags, JSON, markdown, or code fences.\n7. Every UI block must be raw, not markdown fenced/quoted/CDATA-wrapped, and must contain one complete valid JSON object with escaped quotes/newlines in string values and command payloads.\n\nMESSAGE LIST JSON AND ITEM RULES:\n- The info display JSON must contain `\"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\"` exactly and use the local top-level wrapper shape (`title`, `patternId`, optional `description`, and `properties`); do not use `config`:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"<topic> reviewed\",\n    \"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\",\n    \"description\": \"<PREPARED.rejectionSummary>\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"subtitle\": \"<PREPARED.rejectSubtitle>\",\n      \"summary\": \"<PREPARED.rejectionSummary>\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Rejection reason\",\n          \"summary\": \"<rejectionReason>\",\n          \"priority\": \"warning\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n- `properties.items` must be an array of item objects.\n- Each item must include `title`.\n- Supported item fields are only: `title`, `subtitle`, `summary`, `status`, `statusPriority`, `badgeText`, `priority`, `timestamp`, `action`, `additionalAction`, and `image`.\n- Valid `priority` and `statusPriority` values are: `alert`, `warning`, `medium`, `success`, `neutral`.\n- Copy each prepared `priority` and `statusPriority` exactly where used; do not swap or recalculate them.\n- `badgeText` must be a short text label. Do not use a badge object in a messageListWidget item.\n- `statusPriority` styles the `status` text only; item badge styling comes from `priority`.\n- `additionalAction`, when present, must contain only `text` and `command`.\n- Preserve prepared `action` and `additionalAction.command` strings exactly. Do not rebuild command payloads.\n- Include `image` only when the source DATA/PREPARED item provides a non-empty image URL or path. Do not invent image URLs, and do not use emoji or Unicode icons as image substitutes.\n- Omit empty optional fields instead of outputting null, empty objects, or unsupported fields.\n- <topic> must be 2 to 4 words in Title Case derived from ChangeRequestSummary.\n- Derive ChangeRequestSummary from these sources in order:\n  1) UPDATE_RESULT parts item `fetchRejectedPolicyDeviation` -> payload/result -> ChangeRequestSummary\n  2) PREPARED.changeRequestSummary\n  3) ACTION_CONTEXT.changeRequestSummary\n  4) ACTION_CONTEXT.issueText\n- description and properties.summary must exactly equal PREPARED.rejectionSummary.\n- properties.subtitle must exactly equal PREPARED.rejectSubtitle when present.\n- <rejectionReason> must use the exact submitted editor text from ACTION_CONTEXT.newValue when available; otherwise use PREPARED.rejectionReason.\n- Do not add unsupported fields.\n\nEDIT REASON INSIGHT RULES:\n- Return exactly one ordinary insight after the policy_rejection info display and before the immediate insight.\n- `title` must be exactly `Edit Reason`.\n- `actionText` must be exactly `Edit Reason`.\n- `shortDescription` must be one concise sentence saying the rejection reason can be updated.\n- `followUpCommand` must be exactly in this command format:\n  ora.Invoke('RejectRecommendation', <payload-object>)\n- Build the payload object by copying PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase exactly, then add exactly one key:\n  - \"value\": \"<current rejection reason>\"\n- <current rejection reason> must use the exact submitted editor text from ACTION_CONTEXT.newValue when available; otherwise use PREPARED.rejectionReason.\n- Do not rebuild or modify PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase.id.\n- Do not change the form id, type, title, subtitle, or commitText from PREPARED.rejectFormPayloadBase.\n- Saving the reopened form must return to the same reject update and CONFIRM_REJECT_ISSUE confirmation flow.\n\nIMMEDIATE REFRESH RULES:\n- Return exactly one immediate insight after the Edit Reason insight.\n- The immediate insight must be exactly:\n<oraImmediateInsight>\n{\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"RefreshPanel\\\")\"\n}\n</oraImmediateInsight>\n- Do not add title, shortDescription, actionText, or any other fields to the immediate insight.\n- Do not change the RefreshPanel action code."
            },
